  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Veerapuneni Venkayyavenkanna vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh on 15 October, 2019 Author: U. Durga Prasad Rao Bench: U. Durga Prasad Rao Hon'Ble Sri Justice U. Durga Prasad Rao Criminal Petition No.6141 of 2019 Order:",
    "facts": "The petitioners/A1 & A3 seek to quash the proceedings against them in Crime No.556 of 2019 of Gajuwaka Police Station, Visakhapatnam, registered for the offences under Sections 188, 273, 328 r/w 34 IPC and Section 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act (for short, 'FSS Act'). 2. The allegations against the petitioners briefly are that on 26.09.2019 at 13.00 hours, when the complainant along with his staff conducting ride at D.No.7-6-25, near Durga temple, Kandipalli Street, Pedagantyada, on suspicion, caught A2 and found banned tobacco products in his possession and on interrogation, A2 revealed the involvement of A1, A3 & A4 and hence, arrested A2 & A4 and seized the same and registered a case in Crime No.556 of 2019 of Gajuwaka Police Station, Visakhapatnam for the offences stated supra.",
    "arguments": "3. Learned counsel for petitioners while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act. He relied upon the order of this Court in Crl.P.Nos.3731 of 2018 and batch, dated 27.08.2018.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "3. Learned counsel for petitioners while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act. He relied upon the order of this Court in Crl.P.Nos.3731 of 2018 and batch, dated 27.08.2018.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
